  "paragraph": 30,
  "text": "Zooming out to production deployments, this exact same core harness engine powers two major topologies today. On the left are interactive local harnesses like Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Cursor, Windsurf, OpenCode, Aider, and Cline. Those are built for low-latency pairing right inside your terminal or editor. On the right are headless cloud background harnesses like Devin, Codex Cloud, GitHub Copilot, Cursor Background Agents, and OpenHands. They pull tickets from a queue, spin up fresh containers, run checks, and open pull requests while you focus elsewhere.",
